From 6649776502ac5769a07c1693e75c5af7b5206eb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:59:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable DTD processing in the lazy SOAP body StAX parser

EnvelopeFactory.parseEnvelopeStax() parses the SOAP envelope when an
application sets the saaj.lazy.soap.body property. It created its
shared XMLInputFactory with XMLInputFactory.newInstance() and set no
security properties, so a DOCTYPE in the envelope was processed. An
external entity could read a local file or make the server fetch a
URL, and nested internal entities could exhaust CPU and memory
(CWE-611, CWE-776). The default SAX path already rejects any DOCTYPE
with RejectDoctypeSaxFilter. The StAX path had no such guard.

The factory now has SUPPORT_DTD and IS_SUPPORTING_EXTERNAL_ENTITIES set
to false before it is stored in the static field. The parser no longer
reads the declarations in a DOCTYPE, so it does not resolve external
entities or expand internal ones. A reference to an entity declared in a
DOCTYPE now fails the parse. Envelopes without a DOCTYPE, the default
SAX path and readers passed in through a StAXSource are unchanged.

Adds LazyStaxXXETest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-76vm-gg49-hx7p
